    "https://www.jobs.gla.ac.uk/job/centre-co-ordinator-6045416": {
      "title": "Centre Co-Ordinator · University of Glasgow",
      "description": "Centre Co-Ordinator · University of Glasgow This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. read more Got it! Vacancies About Us Contact Why UofG Login Register Login Menu Vacancies About Us Why UofG Contact Sign In Home Jobs Centre Co-Ordinator Centre Co-Ordinator Back to jobs Centre Co-Ordinator Job details Posted 01 October 2026 Salary Grade 6, £33,951 - £37,694 per annum pro rata Location Garscube Job Type Management Professional & Administrative Reference 207933 Expiry 22 Oct 2026 23:45 Job description Job Purpose The Scottish Brain Tumour Research Centre of Excellence is a collaborative initiative between the Universities of Glasgow and Edinburgh that brings together researchers, clinicians, technical specialists, students, patient representatives and external partners to accelerate the development of novel therapies for glioblastoma. The Centre supports translational research, training and development, patient and public involvement, industry engagement and collaborative funding development across both institutions. The postholder will support the operational delivery of the Centre's activities by coordinating projects, events, reporting processes, communications and stakeholder engagement activities across Glasgow and Edinburgh. Acting as a central point of contact, the role will facilitate collaboration across partner organisations, support the development of funding opportunities and ensure effective delivery of Centre objectives. The role will work closely with the Centre Directors, investigators, professional services teams, patient representatives and external partners to support the continued growth, visibility and impact of the Centre. Main Duties and Responsibilities 1.     Coordinate the delivery of activities across the Scottish Brain Tumour Research Centre of Excellence, supporting progress against agreed objectives, milestones and deliverables. 2.     Maintain project documentation, action logs and delivery schedules, monitoring progress against agreed timelines and following up actions with relevant stakeholders. 3.     Support effective collaboration between the Universities of Glasgow and Edinburgh by coordinating communications, meetings and shared activities across Centre workstreams and stakeholder groups. 4.     Identify emerging issues that may impact delivery and escalate these appropriately to Centre leadership, proposing solutions where relevant. 5.     Collect, collate and analyse information on Centre activities, outputs, outcomes and impact measures, preparing reports, presentations and briefing materials for Centre Directors, funders, governance groups and other stakeholders. 6.     Coordinate the delivery of Centre workshops, seminars, annual meetings, training activities and networking events, involving researchers, students, patient representatives, external partners and stakeholders. 7.     Co-ordinate Patient and Public Involvement and Engagement (PPIE) activities, including meetings with patient representatives, public engagement events and communication with Centre supporters. 8.     Support funding development activities by coordinating grant preparation processes, collating information from investigators and tracking funding opportunities, highlighting such opportunities to Centre Directors for awareness and action. 9.     Maintain engagement with industry and external partners, coordinating meetings and facilitating communication with relevant University professional services teams, including contracts, knowledge exchange and research support functions. 10.  Support dissemination of Centre activities and achievements through websites, newsletters, conference submissions, social media and other communication channels. 11.  Monitor Centre activities and gather information on outputs, outcomes and impact measures to support reporting and future funding applications. 12.  Act as a key point of contact for Centre operations, maintaining effective working relationships across partner institutions and ensuring activities are undertaken in accordance with relevant University policies and procedures. 13.  Undertake any other reasonable duties commensurate with the grade of the post. Knowledge, Qualifications, Skills and Experience Knowledge/Qualifications Essential A1. Scottish Credit and Qualifications Framework (SCQF) Level 8 (Scottish Vocational Qualification level 4, Higher National Diploma) or equivalent professional qualification, or relevant experience in  project management, programme coordination, research management or a related area. A2. Working knowledge of project management principles and techniques, including planning, monitoring, risk management and reporting. A3. Understanding of collaborative research, higher education, healthcare, public sector or charitable research environments. A4. Knowledge of stakeholder engagement and partnership working. Desirable: B1. Professional project management qualification   (e.g. PRINCE2 Foundation, Agile, APM or equivalent). B2. Knowledge of biomedical, translational or clinical research environments. B3. Understanding of Patient and Public Involvement and Engagement (PPIE). Skills Essential: C1. Excellent project coordination and organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple activities simultaneously. C2. Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to communicate effectively with a broad range of stakeholders. C3. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to develop productive working relationships across institutions and disciplines. C4. Ability to organise meetings, workshops, training events and stakeholder engagement activities. C5. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to identify issues and implement practical solutions. C6. Ability to prepare reports, briefings, presentations and project documentation to a high standard. C7. Experience using Microsoft 365 applications and online collaboration tools. C8. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as part of a multidisciplinary team. C9. Ability to prioritise workload effectively and meet competing deadlines. Desirable: D1 Academic/Industry research skills and background in genetics/molecular biology/clinical operations/oncology. Experience Essential: E1. Experience supporting or delivering projects involving multiple stakeholders and workstreams. E2. Experience organising meetings, events, workshops or training activities. E3. Experience maintaining project records and preparing reports or management information. E4. Experience working collaboratively across teams and organisational boundaries. E5. Experience supporting stakeholder engagement and partnership activities. Desirable: F1. Experience working within a university, NHS, research institute or charity-funded research environment. F2. Experience supporting collaborative research programmes. F3. Experience coordinating Patient and Public Involvement and Engagement activities. F4. Experience supporting industry partnerships, knowledge exchange activities or research funding applications. F5. Experience supporting funding applications or research grant development. F6. Experience supporting research communications, public engagement or dissemination activities. Informal enquiries should be directed to Anthony Chalmers, Anthony.Chalmers@glasgow.ac.uk Terms and Conditions Salary will be Grade 6, £33,951 - £37,694 per annum pro rata. The grade for this position is Grade 6, £33,951 - £37,694 per annum pro rata. Please note that due to limited funding availability for this position, the salary range on offer is up to £36,636 per annum pro rata (Grade 6, spinal point 28) This post is part-time (21 hours per week) and fixed term until up to 31 October 2029. The University of Glasgow has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK, please note that this post won't eligible to be sponsored under the Skilled Worker visa route. As a valued member of our team, you can expect: 1 A warm welcoming and engaging organisational culture, where your talents are developed and nurtured, and success is celebrated and shared. 2 An excellent employment package with generous terms and conditions including 41 days of leave for full time staff, pension - pensions handbook https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/payandpensions/pensions/, benefits and discount packages. 3 A flexible approach to working. 4 A commitment to support your health and wellbeing, including a free 6-month UofG Sport membership for all new staff joining the University  https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/staff/healthwellbeing/. We believe that we can only reach our full potential through the talents of all. Equality, diversity and inclusion are at the heart of our values. Applications are particularly welcome from across our communities and in particular people from the Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic (BAME) community, and other protected characteristics who are under-represented within the University. Read more on how the University promotes and embeds all aspects of equality and diversity within our community https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/humanresources/equalitydiversity/. We endorse the principles of Athena Swan https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/humanresources/equalitydiversity/athenaswan/ and hold bronze, silver and gold awards across the University. We are investing in our organisation, and we will invest in you too. Please visit our website https://www.gla.ac.uk/explore/jobs/ for more information. Closing Date: 22 October 2026 at 23:45 Apply Now Save this job Centre Co-Ordinator Posted 11 days ago Apply Now Share this job linkedin twitter facebook mail whatsapp Sign up for job alerts Sign in or register here to receive emails about new jobs like these You agree to our Terms & conditions Latest Jobs Research Associate in Evidence Synthesis Glasgow GRADE 7, £41,064-£46,049 per annum People and OD (HR) Systems Coordinator Glasgow Grade 6, £33,951 - £37,694 per annum Research Associate - Applied Research & Knowledge Exchange Glasgow Grade 7:  £41,064 - £46,049 per annum Research Associate - Delivering Humanised Places Glasgow Grade 7:  £41,064 - £46,049 per annum Project Manager Glasgow £41,064 pa - £46,049 pa logo The University of Glasgow is a registered Scottishcharity: Registration Number SC004401 X Facebook instagram Legal Cookies Terms of use PeopleXD accessibilty statement Candidate privacy notice Accreditation Quick Links About Contact Us Vacancies Salaries Applicant Guide All Right Reserved 2026 University of Glasgow Recruitment website by"
